ff Kingsbury"},{"season":2025,"team":"NYG","distance":0.9794,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Mike Kafka"},{"season":2022,"team":"ARI","distance":0.9825,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Kliff Kingsbury"}],"defense":[{"season":2025,"team":"SEA","distance":0.1824,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Mike Macdonald"},{"season":2023,"team":"CHI","distance":0.2625,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"HOU","distance":0.2709,"shared":4,"play_caller":"DeMeco Ryans"},{"season":2022,"team":"NE","distance":0.2969,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"NO","distance":0.2993,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dennis Allen"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Titans are 1-9 through week 11 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 290 to 197. Neither side has held up so far, with the offense 23rd in EPA per play and the defense 32nd in EPA allowed. What sets them apart is the highest no-huddle rate in the league.","offense":"The Titans offense has been well below average by EPA per play so far. They have been one of the most run-heavy teams in the league, passing less often than game situations would predict. Schematically, they stand out for the highest no-huddle rate and the 2nd highest RPO rate in the league. Cam Ward has run the passing game, with Carnell Tate leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Titans have one of the worst defenses in the league this season, ranking 28th or worse in four of the five main efficiency measures. Even its strongest area, takeaways per game, only ranks 13th, and it is 32nd in EPA allowed per play. Jeffery Simmons has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is Jacob Martin, who has 7.5 sacks while playing only 59% of the snaps, after not being a regular on this defense last season. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is a number of defenders in the box that ranks 6th lowest in the league.","special":"The Titans have been one of the most conservative teams on fourth down, going for it on only 25% of their short-yardage chances. Their kickers have made 95% of field goals, which is one of the best in the league. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the defensive line, about 25% of the money on the books. Their linebackers were among the youngest in the league.","players":"Cam Ward has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,962 yards. Targets have been spread around, with Carnell Tate and Wan'Dale Robinson leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. Tony Pollard has handled most of the work in the backfield with 80% of the carries. On defense, Jacob Martin leads the team with 7.5 sacks and Amani Hooker has picked off 5 passes.","coaching":"Brian Daboll is calling the offense and Robert Saleh is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2023 Colts under Shane Steichen and the 2025 Commanders under Kliff Kingsbury. Their defense looks most like the 2025 Seahawks under Mike Macdonald and the 2023 Bears.","trends":"The offense went from 30th in EPA per play in 2025 to 23rd so far this season, a modest improvement. The defense moved from 28th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 32nd so far this season, a modest decline. The biggest change in approach was two point attempt rate, which went from 0% to 15%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}